c_artifact_references.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-bb[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-bb/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Shared reference-list codec and the ChangeSpec REFS section[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-refs[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-refs: add the Rust parse/normalize/render/batch-resolve API for [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stored artifact-reference lists, expose it through the PyO3 binding, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]teach the Rust ChangeSpec parser the new REFS section behind a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]wire-schema bump.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The bead refs field in the Rust core[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-beads[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-refs[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-beads: give beads a `refs` list with its own add and remove events,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]SQLite column and migration, JSONL codec, `sase bead ref` and `sase bead[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]create --ref` handling, show rendering, search coverage, and doctor [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]diagnostics.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Python bead refs, show, and doctor[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]beads[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-beads[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]beads: raise the core floor, add the Python reference-list facade, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mirror the new bead field across the model, codecs, and JSON wire, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]render a resolved REFS section in `sase bead show`, and thread the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reference context into `sase bead doctor`.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The ChangeSpec REFS section in Python, CLI, and ACE[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]changespecs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after beads[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]changespecs: parse, format, and atomically persist the REFS section in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Python, consolidate the duplicated section-boundary tables onto one [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]constant, add `sase changespec ref`, render REFS in the ACE CLI and TUI,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and add the `sase doctor` validation check.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Published pages, ACE Plans tab, mobile bridge, and declaration[bold black on #87D7FF][/bold #D7AFFF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]surfaces[dim] · [dim][/dim]after beads[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]surfaces: render bead references on published pages and in the ACE Plans[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]detail panel, return them through the mobile bridge, and let `sase [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]artifact create` attach the reference it just minted to a bead.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Documentation, skills, and the live-store audit[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after changespecs, surfaces[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs: document the bead field and the ChangeSpec section, update the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]affected skill sources, regenerate the deployed skills, and audit both [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]live stores with the new validators.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-bb","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","phase_bead_id":"sase-bb.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vc